      "id": 1,
      "text": "Heisson was named after German immigrant Alexander Heisen who homesteaded there in 1866.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heisson%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the post office opened in 1904, it was recorded as 'Heisson' instead of Heisen, a spelling mistake that stuck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heisson%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s post office sits next to a crossing for the historic Chelatchie Prairie Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
